---
# An archived project with nothing left to do is where a walk ends, not a
# deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Archiving a project (POST /api/projects/{slug}/archive) while its
# threads run, its main thread boots, or a message or new thread arrives,
# and what reopening it restores. project_main_threads.fizz archives only
# a project with no thread and no request in flight, and
# archive_unarchive.fizz is one session; nothing else interleaves the
# project archive with threads, their reports, or messages.
#
# Checked against internal/serve:
#   projects.go     archiveProject: main := MainID; ids := projectSessions;
#                   EndProject; then SetArchived(id) for every id, main
#                   last. messageProject: Main; unarchive; Send.
#   supervisor.go   EndProject: EndChild per thread (sorted ids), then
#                   Kill(main); projectSessions = main's children plus every
#                   meta with Project == slug. Main(): the per-slug lock,
#                   the id and its Project meta saved BEFORE Create. MainID:
#                   "" while main's history file does not exist yet.
#                   SetArchived: flag, then Kill. Send/ensure: refuse an
#                   archived session, else spawn `-r id`.
#   children.go     CreateChild: an archived parent is refused unless
#                   Thread (the page's New thread); childEventLocked: a
#                   running child's done/cancelled/exit -> go report ->
#                   notifyFrom(parent). An idle child's exit reports
#                   nothing new (key <= Reported).
#   notify.go       notifyFrom: a live parent gets a stdin notice (which
#                   wakes an idle one into a turn); otherwise a stored
#                   notice. It never starts a process; to a file that
#                   does not exist it is dropped.
#   web/src         project.tsx ProjectHome's composer line "Archived. A
#                   message reopens it."; app.tsx the session composer's
#                   "This session is read-only until unarchived." with Send
#                   disabled.
#
# Fields:
#   setup     "start" until the first step picks the project: "active"
#             (main live and idle, thread t1 running) or "fresh" (no main
#             yet, no thread; the first request boots main).
#   arch      the archive handler's position: idle, ending (EndChild per
#             snapshot thread), killing (EndProject's Kill(main)), flagging
#             (the SetArchived loop, one step: nothing another client does
#             can land between two SetArchived calls that changes an
#             outcome here), done (answered 200).
#   mid       MainID at the handler's start: main had a history file.
#   main      main's process: none, boot (Main's Create waiting for the
#             history file; the child is not in s.kids yet, so Kill cannot
#             reach it), idle, turn.
#   main_arch main's meta.Archived.   main_hist: its history file exists.
#   t1        the thread running at the start: none, running, idle
#             (turn over, process live), dead. t1_arch its flag. It is
#             always in the snapshot.
#   x         the one thread started later: by main's own spawn (x_by
#             "main") or by the page's New thread ("page"). x_snap: it
#             existed when the handler took its snapshot.
#   rep1/repx a report in flight to main (the report goroutine).
#   msg       the one message from the project home: none, boot (it is
#             the request that boots main), sent (written to main's
#             stdin, 200 answered, not yet read), recorded (main took it:
#             an input in main's history), lost (main killed before
#             reading it). lost_by: which step killed it.
#   wake_in   the archive phase in which a thread's report woke main into
#             a turn ("" = never during an archive).
#   left      at the archive's return, what of the project it left live
#             and unarchived: "", "thread" or "main".
#   view      home or main (the page shows main's conversation).
#
# Scope cuts, since every generated path is one browser walk (866
# states): one archive, one message and one later thread per walk, and a
# walk sends the message or starts the page's thread, not both; before
# the archive the only requests are a fresh project's first one (a
# message to an unarchived main is project_main_threads); a fresh
# project is archived only while its main boots; t1 finishes on its own
# only before the archive; main spawns only before it is killed; the
# page opens main only onto an archived, quiet one. The handler's
# MainID/projectSessions and EndProject's own second read of them are one
# snapshot here: nothing modelled changes between the two.
#
# FINDINGS (main 5471918e). The invariants are what the code keeps; each
# broken promise is pinned to the exact window that breaks it.
#   wake     EndProject kills threads before main: each running thread's
#            exit report is a stdin notice to a live main, which wakes
#            into a turn during the archive (wake_in == "ending").
#   escape   that woken main can spawn a thread (CreateChild checks
#            main's flag, not yet set) after the snapshot; it is never
#            ended or flagged and runs on, unarchived, under an archived
#            main (left == "thread"). A page New thread sent during the
#            archive escapes the same way.
#   respawn  archiveProject kills (EndProject) before it flags: a message
#            between Kill(main) and SetArchived(main) finds main
#            unarchived, Send respawns it and answers 200, and
#            SetArchived's own Kill ends it before or after it reads the
#            line (lost_by "flag"). A message during "ending" is killed by
#            EndProject's Kill(main) the same way (lost_by "kill").
#   boot     the mapped model's "main is neither killed nor archived" is
#            half wrong: main's Project meta is saved before Create, so
#            projectSessions lists the booting main and the SetArchived
#            loop flags it. But it is not in s.kids, so neither Kill
#            reaches it: its Create finishes and a live, archived main
#            runs (left == "main"). Booted by a message, messageProject
#            then unarchives it (the message wins); by New thread, the
#            thread starts under the archived main.
#   hidden   New thread on an archived project: Main returns the
#            archived main without unarchiving it, CreateChild(Thread)
#            bypasses the archived parent, and the thread's report is a
#            stored notice in a session the project page calls archived.
#   promise  the home composer says "A message reopens it"; main's own
#            composer, opened from the same page, says read-only and
#            disables Send. Static UI text: the model keeps view only so
#            walks visit an archived main opened on the page.

role Project:
    action Init:
        self.setup = "start"
        self.arch = "idle"
        self.mid = False
        self.main = "none"
        self.main_arch = False
        self.main_hist = False
        self.t1 = "none"
        self.t1_arch = False
        self.x = "none"
        self.x_arch = False
        self.x_by = ""
        self.x_snap = False
        self.rep1 = False
        self.repx = False
        self.msg = "none"
        self.msg_in = ""
        self.reopened = False
        self.lost_by = ""
        self.wake_in = ""
        self.left = ""
        self.view = "home"

    # --- which project the walk starts from.

    atomic action StartActive:
        # Main live and idle, one thread mid-turn.
        require self.setup == "start"
        self.setup = "active"
        self.main = "idle"
        self.main_hist = True
        self.t1 = "running"

    atomic action StartFresh:
        # A project with no main thread yet.
        require self.setup == "start"
        self.setup = "fresh"

    # --- threads and their reports.

    atomic action ThreadFinish:
        # t1's turn ends on its own; the report goroutine starts.
        # Scope: before the archive; during it, EndThreads ends it.
        require self.t1 == "running" and self.arch == "idle"
        self.t1 = "idle"
        self.rep1 = True

    atomic action XFinish:
        require self.x == "running"
        self.x = "idle"
        self.repx = True

    atomic fair action Report1:
        require self.rep1
        self.rep1 = False
        deliver(self)

    atomic fair action ReportX:
        require self.repx
        self.repx = False
        deliver(self)

    # --- main.

    atomic fair action MainTurnEnds:
        require self.main == "turn"
        self.main = "idle"

    atomic action MainSpawnsThread:
        # tools.spawn in main's turn: CreateChild(SpawnedBy=main), refused
        # only once main's flag is set.
        require self.main == "turn" and not self.main_arch and self.x == "none"
        # Scope: before main is killed; a reopened main's spawn is normal.
        require self.arch in ("idle", "ending", "killing")
        self.x = "running"
        self.x_by = "main"
        self.x_snap = False

    atomic fair action MainBooted:
        # Main's history file appears; Create claims the child and the
        # request that booted it goes on: messageProject unarchives and
        # Sends; createProjectSession starts the thread (Thread bypasses
        # an archived parent).
        require self.main == "boot"
        self.main = "idle"
        self.main_hist = True
        if self.msg == "boot":
            if self.main_arch:
                self.reopened = True
            self.main_arch = False
            self.msg = "sent"
        else:
            self.x = "running"
            self.x_by = "page"
            self.x_snap = False

    atomic fair action TakeMessage:
        # Main reads the line: an input in its history, a turn.
        require self.msg == "sent" and self.main in ("idle", "turn")
        self.msg = "recorded"
        self.main = "turn"

    # --- the page.

    atomic action MessageProject:
        # The home composer (or another client) POSTs a message.
        require self.setup != "start" and self.msg == "none" and self.view == "home"
        require self.main != "boot"
        # Scope: before the archive only as the fresh project's first
        # message (a message to an unarchived main is project_main_threads).
        require self.arch != "idle" or self.setup == "fresh"
        # Scope: a walk sends the message or starts the page's thread, not
        # both.
        require self.x_by != "page"
        self.msg_in = self.arch
        if not self.main_hist:
            # Main mints the id, saves its Project meta, and Creates.
            self.main = "boot"
            self.msg = "boot"
        else:
            if self.main_arch:
                self.reopened = True
            self.main_arch = False
            if self.main == "none":
                self.main = "idle"
            self.msg = "sent"

    atomic action NewThread:
        # 'New thread' -> createProjectSession: Main, then
        # CreateChild(Thread=true), which ignores main's flag.
        require self.setup != "start" and self.x == "none" and self.view == "home"
        require self.main != "boot" and self.msg == "none"
        require self.arch != "idle" or self.setup == "fresh"
        if not self.main_hist:
            self.main = "boot"
        else:
            self.x = "running"
            self.x_by = "page"
            self.x_snap = False

    atomic action OpenMain:
        # Scope: only onto an archived main, quiet after the archive.
        require self.view == "home" and self.main_hist and self.main_arch
        require self.arch == "done" and not self.rep1 and not self.repx
        require self.msg == "none"
        self.view = "main"

    atomic action Back:
        require self.view == "main"
        self.view = "home"

    # --- the archive handler.

    atomic action ArchiveProject:
        # MainID and projectSessions: the snapshot.
        require self.setup != "start" and self.arch == "idle"
        # Scope: a fresh project is archived only while its main boots.
        require self.setup == "active" or self.main == "boot"
        self.arch = "ending"
        self.mid = self.main_hist
        self.x_snap = self.x != "none"

    atomic fair action EndThreads:
        # EndChild per snapshot thread: a running one is killed and its
        # exit reports; an idle one's exit reports nothing new.
        require self.arch == "ending"
        if self.t1 == "running":
            self.rep1 = True
        if self.t1 != "none":
            self.t1 = "dead"
        if self.x_snap:
            if self.x == "running":
                self.repx = True
            self.x = "dead"
        self.arch = "killing"

    atomic fair action KillMain:
        # EndProject's Kill(main): main only if it is in s.kids.
        require self.arch == "killing"
        kill_main(self, "kill")
        self.arch = "flagging"

    atomic fair action FlagAll:
        # SetArchived(id, true) for the snapshot threads, then main (listed
        # by MainID, or through its Project meta while it boots): flag,
        # then Kill.
        require self.arch == "flagging"
        if self.t1 != "none":
            self.t1_arch = True
        if self.x_snap:
            self.x_arch = True
        self.main_arch = True
        kill_main(self, "flag")
        if self.x in ("running", "idle") and not self.x_arch:
            self.left = "thread"
        elif self.main == "boot":
            self.left = "main"
        self.arch = "done"

def deliver(p):
    # notifyFrom(main): a stdin notice to a live main (waking an idle one),
    # else a stored notice; nothing for a main still booting (t1's reports
    # go to a main with history; x exists only once main does).
    if p.main == "idle":
        p.main = "turn"
        if p.arch != "idle" and p.arch != "done" and p.wake_in == "":
            p.wake_in = p.arch

def kill_main(p, by):
    if p.main in ("idle", "turn"):
        p.main = "none"
        if p.msg == "sent":
            p.msg = "lost"
            p.lost_by = by

action Init:
    project = Project()

def live(state):
    return state in ("running", "idle")

# The snapshot's threads are always ended and flagged by the time the
# archive answers.
always assertion SnapshotEnded:
    if project.arch != "done":
        return True
    t1_ok = project.t1 == "none" or (project.t1 == "dead" and project.t1_arch)
    x_ok = not project.x_snap or (project.x == "dead" and project.x_arch)
    return t1_ok and x_ok

# When the archive answers, nothing of the project is live and unarchived
# except through the two known windows: a thread started after the
# snapshot (escape), or a main still booting (boot).
always assertion ArchiveLeavesNothingLive:
    if project.left == "thread":
        return not project.x_snap
    if project.left == "main":
        return not project.mid
    return True

# The archive flags main, even one still booting.
always assertion ArchiveFlagsMain:
    if project.arch != "done":
        return True
    return project.main_arch or project.reopened

# Flag-before-kill is broken only by Send: once EndProject has killed
# main, nothing but the message restarts it before the flags land (a
# report never starts a process).
always assertion OnlySendRespawnsMainMidArchive:
    if project.arch == "flagging" and project.mid and project.main in ("idle", "turn"):
        return project.msg in ("sent", "recorded")
    return True

# A report wakes main during the archive only while main is live: before
# EndProject's Kill(main) (the "wake" finding), or after it only in a main
# the message respawned (the "respawn" finding) or one that finished
# booting after it (the "boot" finding). A report never starts a process
# itself.
always assertion ReportWakesOnlyALiveMain:
    if project.wake_in == "flagging":
        return project.msg_in == "flagging" or not project.mid
    return True

# A /message answered 200 is recorded on main unless the archive's own
# Kill ended main first (the "respawn" finding).
always assertion MessageLostOnlyToArchiveKill:
    if project.msg == "lost":
        return project.lost_by in ("kill", "flag")
    return True

# A live thread under an archived main that is itself unarchived is always
# one the archive never saw: the page's New thread (hidden) or a spawn
# after the snapshot (escape).
always assertion LiveThreadUnderArchivedMainIsKnown:
    if project.main_arch and live(project.x) and not project.x_arch:
        return project.x_by == "page" or not project.x_snap
    return True

# The home's promise: a message sent to an archived project reopens main
# and main reads it.
always assertion MessageReopens:
    if project.msg_in == "done" and project.msg in ("sent", "recorded"):
        return not project.main_arch and project.reopened
    return True

# The archive request finishes.
always eventually assertion ArchiveCompletes:
    return project.arch in ("idle", "done")

# Main boots, and a message sent to it is read or killed, never stuck.
always eventually assertion MessageSettles:
    return project.msg not in ("boot", "sent")

# Every report reaches main (as a stdin notice or a stored one).
always eventually assertion ReportsLand:
    return not project.rep1 and not project.repx
